---
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro'
import TextPage from '../layouts/TextPage.astro'

/**
 * Short on purpose, like the privacy policy. With no purchase, no subscription
 * and no account, most of a terms page has nothing to attach to. What survives
 * is the licence, the warranty disclaimer it carries, where builds come from,
 * who owns the pictures, and the name.
 */
const updatedLabel = '15 September 2026'
---

<TextPage
  title="Terms of Service | SpreadPaper"
  description="SpreadPaper is free software under the MIT licence. Use it, change it, sell it. No warranty, no account, no small print worth the name."
  socialDescription="Free software under the MIT licence. Use it, read it, fork it, ship it. No warranty."
  eyebrow="Terms"
  heading="Do what you like with it"
  lead="SpreadPaper is free software under the MIT licence. No purchase, no subscription, no account, so most of what a terms page usually covers has nothing here to attach to."
  updated={updatedLabel}
>
  <Prose>
    <h2>The licence is the agreement</h2>
    <p>
      The app and its source are <a
        href="https://github.com/spreadpaper/SpreadPaper/blob/main/LICENSE">MIT licensed</a
      >. Use it, change it, redistribute it, sell it, as long as the copyright notice travels with
      it. If this page ever seems to disagree with the licence, the licence wins.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty, and I mean it</h2>
    <p>
      Provided as is, with no warranty of any kind, and nobody liable for anything that follows from
      using it. That is the licence's own wording and it is meant literally: this is one person's
      evenings, not a support contract. Some places forbid excluding certain warranties, in which
      case that part is not yours to worry about.
    </p>

    <h2>Get it from GitHub</h2>
    <p>
      Official builds live on the <a href="https://github.com/spreadpaper/SpreadPaper/releases"
        >releases page</a
      >, which is where every download button here points. A copy from anywhere else was not built
      by me and could be anything at all.
    </p>

    <h2>Your pictures are yours</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing is claimed over the images you open or the wallpapers made from them, and nothing is
      uploaded. Holding the right to use a given photograph is your department. The ones bundled as
      examples come from Unsplash under the <a href="https://unsplash.com/license"
        >Unsplash licence</a
      >, credited in the footer.
    </p>

    <h2>Forks and pull requests</h2>
    <p>
      Both welcome. Anything you contribute arrives under the same MIT licence so it can ship with
      the project, and issues are public, so leave out anything you would rather keep. Fork it by all
      means, but give yours its own name, so nobody downloads a build expecting this one.
    </p>

    <h2>The small print</h2>
    <p>
      Made by <a href="https://robinvanbaalen.nl">Robin van Baalen</a> in Curaçao, Dutch Caribbean.
      Curaçao law applies, without affecting any consumer rights you have where you live. Reach me
      at <a href="mailto:hello@spreadpaper.app">hello@spreadpaper.app</a>. If any of this changes,
      so does the date at the top.
    </p>

    <p class="see-also">
      See also the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</TextPage>
